  "conclusions": [
    "Doubling the evaluated NVVDD IDDQ input coincided with a reversible 120000-uV reduction in calculated REL, ALT_REL and effective policy on both reported rails. Voltage offsets, reported boost and requested clocks were unchanged.",
    "At matched adjacent idle observations, rows 9/10 record 0 first two raw DWORDs increased to 3118/3898; baseline values were 1547-1549/1934-1936 and restored values 1569/1961. This supports an intervention-associated software response under the recorded conditions.",
    "Only six of sixteen B samples matched the recorded reference; ten mismatches remain captured. All sixteen samples in each A phase matched. Baseline/restored values drifted, so this is not an exact equation or identical baseline distribution."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Telemetry is adjacent, not simultaneous, and samples may share cached values. Hotspot readings changed from 40 C in A1 to 42 C in A2.",
    "The immediate-post-restart v5 comparison had P8/P0 confounding and 32 caught operating-power getter access-violation exceptions; it is not the matched comparison. Fresh sampling children in v6 recorded no telemetry exceptions.",
    "Current type0C raw field units, provider and rail roles, numerical producer and direct causal path remain unqualified. Historical tuple names and arithmetic consistency are insufficient.",
    "No physical power/current/voltage effect or enforcement, arbitrary six-word voltage replay, live 16-byte VFE encoding or modern F219 setter is established.",
    "No new recovery/Undo or saved-profile restoration/replay integration was implemented. Existing transaction cleanup removed the experiment. No Windows reboot, NVIDIA App, driver installation, release or tag operation."
  ],
  "product_change": "The existing IDDQ field details and preview now disclose possible calculated-voltage-limit effects on linked rails; control and receipt contracts are unchanged.",
